{"title": "Components/Text Field/Text Field", "docs": {"text": "TextField\nAccessible AA\nWeb\nAndroid\niOS\nFlutter\nCMP\n\u26a0\ufe0f TextField Component Update\n\nThe component previously known as ODSTextField has been deprecated and renamed to ODSTextFieldDeprecated. A new, improved version of ODSTextField has been introduced with updated APIs and consistent styling with the latest ODS design guidelines.\n\nThe TextField component has been upgraded to follow the latest ODS design and API standards. The previous API is now deprecated and will be removed in an upcoming release. To ensure compatibility and benefit from new features, please migrate your usage to the new API.\n\nA detailed migration guide is available here. You can also run the automated migration script to update your codebase:\n\nnpx --package @telekom-ods/migration@latest migrate-textfield src/your-project-folder\n\nLabel\n\n\nShow code\nCopy code\nODSTextField extends the native HTMLInputElement properties as React props. On top of the additional properties that are listed below, you can also pass the native HTMLInputElement properties as React props. You can read more about those properties here.\n\n\nName\tDescription\tDefault\tControl\nsize\t\nSet the size of the textfield.\n\"small\"\n\"large\"\n\"large\"\nsize\n\nsmall\n\nlarge\nmode\t\nTo show an icon with a message below the input field. Default value is informative.\n\"error\"\n\"standard\"\n\"informative\"\n\"standard\"\nmode\n\nerror\n\nstandard\n\ninformative\nrequired\t\nWhether the TextField is required. Adds aria-required and shows a required indicator next to the Label.\n\nboolean\nfalse\nSet boolean\nshowAsterisk\t\nWhether to show the required asterisk indicator (*) next to the label. When provided, takes precedence over the deprecated required prop for asterisk visibility. To also mark the field as required for form validation and accessibility, pass inputProps={{ required: true }}.\n\nboolean\n-\tSet boolean\ndisabled\t\nWhether the input is disabled. Disables interaction and applies a disabled style.\nboolean\nfalse\nSet boolean\nreadonly\t\nWhether the input is read-only. Prevents changes but allows focus and text selection.\nboolean\nfalse\nSet boolean\nplaceholderText\t\nPlaceholder text displayed inside the input when it's empty.\nstring\n-\t\n\nshowCounter\t\nWhether to show a character counter below the input field. If an inputProps.maxLength value is provided, then the counter text will have the format of XX/YY (eg. 12/40). Otherwise the actual lenght of the input will be displayed as a singe number.\n\nboolean\nfalse\nSet boolean\nleftIconValue\t\nThe left icon.\nReactNode\n-\t\n\nleftIconValue :{\n$$typeof : Symbol(react.transitional.element)\ntype : function(e){var r=e.size,t=e.fill,l=t===void 0?\"currentColor\":t,a=e.color,m=a===void 0?\"currentColor\":a,d=e.selected,j=d===void 0?!1:d,c=e.decorative,g=c===void 0?!1:c,v=e.title,o=e.accessibilityTitle,h=e.description,f=e.focusable,x=f===void 0?!1:f,u=e.small,n=u===void 0?!1:u,b=e.className,z=V(e,[\"size\",\"fill\",\"color\",\"selected\",\"decorative\",\"title\",\"accessibilityTitle\",\"description\",\"focusable\",\"small\",\"className\"]),p=r||(n?16:24);return o&&console.warn(\"The `accessibilityTitle` prop is deprecated and will be removed in a future version. Please use `title` instead.\"),i.jsxs(\"svg\",s({className:[\"ODSIcon\",b].filter(Boolean).join(\" \"),xmlns:\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\",width:p,height:p,viewBox:n?\"0 0 16 16\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"aria-hidden\":!!g,tabIndex:x?0:-1},z,{children:[(v||o)&&i.jsx(\"title\",{children:v||o}),h&&i.jsx(\"desc\",{children:h}),i.jsx(\"g\",{fill:l===\"currentColor\"?m:l,children:j?n?i.jsx(\"g\",{children:i.jsx(\"path\",{clipRule:\"evenodd\",fillRule:\"evenodd\",d:\"M4.502 2a.6.6 0 0 0-.6.6V4h-2.3a.6.6 0 0 0-.6.6v1.102A3.5 3.5 0 0 0 4.48 9.2a4.1 4.1 0 0 0 2.92 1.956V12.8H5A.6.6 0 1 0 5 14h6a.6.6 0 0 0 0-1.2H8.6v-1.643A4.1 4.1 0 0 0 11.525 9.2a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 3.471-3.498V4.6a.6.6 0 0 0-.6-.6h-2.294V2.6a.6.6 0 0 0-.6-.6zm7.6 3.2v1.9q-.001.433-.086.841a2.3 2.3 0 0 0 1.78-2.24V5.2zm-9.9 0h1.7v1.9q0 .433.087.843a2.3 2.3 0 0 1-1.787-2.241z\"})}):i.jsx(\"g\",{children:i.jsx(\"path\",{clipRule:\"evenodd\",fillRule:\"evenodd\",d:\"M7 3a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v1H3a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v2a5 5 0 0 0 4.8 4.996 6 6 0 0 0 4.203 2.922L11 16v3H8a1 1 0 1 0 0 2h8a1 1 0 1 0 0-2h-3v-3q0-.042-.003-.082a6 6 0 0 0 4.203-2.922A5 5 0 0 0 22 8V6a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-3V4a1 1 0 0 0-1-1zm13 5a3 3 0 0 1-2.06 2.85q.06-.417.06-.85V7h2zM6.06 10.85A6 6 0 0 1 6 10V7H4v1c0 1.328.863 2.455 2.06 2.85\"})}):n?i.jsx(\"g\",{children:i.jsx(\"path\",{clipRule:\"evenodd\",fillRule:\"evenodd\",d:\"M4.502 2a.6.6 0 0 0-.6.6V4h-2.3a.6.6 0 0 0-.6.6v1.102A3.5 3.5 0 0 0 4.48 9.2a4.1 4.1 0 0 0 2.92 1.956V12.8H5A.6.6 0 1 0 5 14h6a.6.6 0 0 0 0-1.2H8.6v-1.643A4.1 4.1 0 0 0 11.525 9.2a3.5 3.5 0 0 0 3.471-3.498V4.6a.6.6 0 0 0-.6-.6h-2.294V2.6a.6.6 0 0 0-.6-.6zm6.4 2.525a.6.6 0 0 0 0 .15V7.1a2.9 2.9 0 1 1-5.8 0V3.2h5.8zm1.2.675h1.694v.502a2.3 2.3 0 0 1-1.78 2.24q.086-.409.086-.842zm-9.9 0h1.7v1.9q0 .433.087.843a2.3 2.3 0 0 1-1.787-2.241z\"})}):i.jsx(\"g\",{children:i.jsx(\"path\",{clipRule:\"evenodd\",fillRule:\"evenodd\",d:\"M7 3a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v1H3a1 1 0 0 0-1 1v2a5 5 0 0 0 4.8 4.996 6 6 0 0 0 4.203 2.922L11 16v3H8a1 1 0 1 0 0 2h8a1 1 0 1 0 0-2h-3v-3q0-.042-.003-.082a6 6 0 0 0 4.203-2.922A5 5 0 0 0 22 8V6a1 1 0 0 0-1-1h-3V4a1 1 0 0 0-1-1zm9 2H8v5a4 4 0 0 0 8 0zm2 2h2v1a3 3 0 0 1-2.06 2.85q.06-.417.06-.85zM4 7h2v3q0 .433.06.85A3 3 0 0 1 4 8z\"})})})]}))}\nkey : null\nref : null\nprops :{...} 1 key\n}\nprefixText\t\nThe prefix text for the input value, typically used for currency symbols.\nstring\n-\tSet string\nsuffixText\t\nThe suffix text for the input value, typically used for units of measure.\nstring\n-\tSet string\nlabelText*\t\nThe label of the input field.\nstring\n-\t\n\nsupportMessageProps\t\nProps for displaying support messages such as helper text.\nODSSupportMessageProps\n-\t\n\nsupportMessageProps :{\nhelperText : \"Support Message\"\n}\nshowRightIcon\t\nWhether to display a right-side icon inside the TextField. Defaults to false; set to true when providing textFieldIconProps with an icon or buttonProps.buttonIcon.\n\nboolean\nfalse\nFalseTrue\ntextFieldIconProps\t\nAdditional props to customize the right side icon used inside the TextField.\nODSTextFieldIconProps\n-\t\n\ntextFieldIconProps :{\ntype : \"buttonContainer\"\nbuttonProps :{...} 1 key\nicon :{...} 5 keys\n}\ninputProps\t\nProps to apply directly to the underlying <input> element. value and defaultValue are excluded.\nOmit<ODSComponentPropsWithRef<\"input\">, \"defaultValue\" | \"value\">\n-\t\n\ninputProps :{\nmaxLength : 40\n}\nAPI Reference\n\nWhile the ODSTextField provides inputProps to apply the native input properties directly to the underlying <input> element, in order to use the component in a controlled manner you should use the value and defaultValue props that are explicitly defined in the properties.\n\n<ODSTextField\n    labelText=\"label\"\n    value={value} // handle the value from here\n    defaultValue={'Init value'} // handle the defaultValue from here\n    inputProps={{ onChange: (e) => setValue(e.target.value) }} // handle the change event from here\n/>\nCopy\nGeneral\n\nA text field allows users to enter a single line of text.\n\nWhen to use:\n\nUse input fields when users should enter information like:\n\nEmail addresses\nPasswords\nPhone numbers\nDate, month, week and time\nAny other kind of information as free text\nWhen not to use:\n\nDon't use a text field when users need to:\n\nsearch for something (here use the search component) or\nenter more than one line of input (use a text area instead).\n\nAnatomy\n\n\nUse Directives\n\nHow designers should use the component\n\nType\n\nOption explanations\n\nThe text field component has a lot of options. Here\u2019s a guide to what they can be used for.\n\n\nBest practices\n\nDeclare text fields for specific data formats accordingly (e.g., for types like text, number, email, or password).\nGroup text fields that are related to the same topic.\nArrange input fields in a single-column layout to not disturb the user's editing flow. Exceptions are logically related fields like postal code and city.\nMark mandatory inputs and reduce optional inputs as much as possible.\nExplain all input requirements, for example for passwords or credit card numbers.\nDos and don\u2019ts\n\nLabel overflow\n\nKeep labels concise and scannable. They should not be so long they don\u2019t fit inside the text field.\n\n\nBehaviours\n\nHow the component will behave in a live environment\n\nInput overflow\n\nIf the content is too long for the single line of a text input, then the user can horizontally scroll inside the field either by scrolling or moving the cursor.\n\n\nComponent Variants\n\nLarge\n\nStandard\n\n\nSupport message - Informative\n\n\nSupport message - Error\n\n\nSmall\n\nStandard\n\n\nSupport message - Informative\n\n\nSupport message - Error\n\n\nColour Schemes\n\nHow it works (or is restricted) across colour schemes\n\nWhite\n\n  \nBlack\n\n  \nMagenta\n\nThis component can only be used on neutral colour schemes\n\n  \nSecondary\n\nThis component can only be used on neutral colour schemes\n\n  \nExamples\n\nAdd new address form\n\n\nAccessibility\n\nThis OneDS component is compliant with WCAG 2.2 AA Standards.\n\nKey considerations for keyboard interactions and screen readers are included. Additionally, all components meet requirements for the contrast ratios.\n\nDesign considerations\n\n-Make labels for the field and support messages short and specific, include format information in the labels. -Provide clear error messages (see Support Messages). -A disabled text field must not have a support message, and its label should not convey any crucial information needed to understand the context.\n\nRefer to the AX annotation guide for detailed designer instructions on accessibility annotations.\n\nDevelopment considerations\n\nTextFields and Labels are associated with each other using the\u202ffor\u202fattribute.\nKnown A11y issue in Mobile android app: the textfield has to be activated twice to be edited.\nWhile this individual component is accessible, building fully usable interfaces requires further attention. For guidance, refer to our OneExperience accessibility resources.\n\n", "code": ["", "<ODSTextField\n    labelText=\"label\"\n    value={value} // handle the value from here\n    defaultValue={'Init value'} // handle the defaultValue from here\n    inputProps={{ onChange: (e) => setValue(e.target.value) }} // handle the change event from here\n/>\nCopy\n", "<ODSTextField\n    labelText=\"label\"\n    value={value} // handle the value from here\n    defaultValue={'Init value'} // handle the defaultValue from here\n    inputProps={{ onChange: (e) => setValue(e.target.value) }} // handle the change event from here\n/>\n"], "stories": [{"id": "story--components-textfield--example", "html": "<div id=\"story--components-textfield--example-inner\" data-name=\"Example\" lang=\"en\"><div><div style=\"display: flex; padding: 16px; width: 100%; flex-direction: column; align-items: center;\"><div class=\"ODSColumn ODSTextField\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSTextField-InputField ODSTextField-InputField--size-large ODSTextField-InputField--mode-standard\"><div class=\"ODSColumn ODSTextField-Content ODSTextField-Content--size-large\"><div class=\"ODSRow ODSTextField-Eyebrow\"><label class=\"ODSTextField-Label ODSTextField-Label--size-large ODSTextField-Label--mode-standard\" for=\"_r_19_\">Label</label></div><div class=\"ODSRow ODSTextField-InputContainer ODSTextField-InputContainer--mode-standard\"><svg class=\"ODSIcon ODSTextField-LeftIconValue ODSTextField-LeftIconValue--mode-standard ODSTextField-LeftIconValue--size-large\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" aria-hidden=\"false\" tabindex=\"-1\"><g fill=\"currentColor\"><g><path clip-rule=\"e